      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crownpoint%2C_New_Mexico",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The area that is now Crownpoint was once home to the Anasazi, ancient Pueblo peoples who left cliff dwellings nearby.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://crownpoint.navajochapters.org/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Crownpoint lies along the Trail of the Ancients Byway, a New Mexico Scenic Byway that showcases historic pueblos and desert landscapes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crownpoint%2C_New_Mexico",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Chief Becenti, a Navajo headman, is one of the earliest documented leaders of the Crownpoint area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
